{"role":"assistant","content":"## Ruling: **another compiler revision — D2, the unary token-packet lane**\n\nDo **not** raise the acceptance budget on the current evidence. “Between 2M and 4M” provides no exact per-lane completion counts from which to justify finite headroom, and the remaining map construction/lookup cost is still avoidable.\n\n### Mechanism\n\nReplace D’s three-key map with an ephemeral two-element vector:\n\n```clojure\n[dsg__call_token dsg__args]\n```\n\nThe generated intra-unit helper constructs it with two `conj` operations and applies the **same strictly unary public entry**. The entry recognizes this shape only when element zero equals the compiler-held `dsg__call_token`; on success it applies the private body to element one and forwards the outcome, exactly as D’s authenticated map lane does.\n\nOrdinary public invocation records remain maps and retain their existing `:clj/outcome-token` path. A guest cannot select the vector lane without the unexported token. In particular, raw `[42]`, `[nil [42]]`, or another forged vector receives no private access.\n\nThis preserves:\n\n- one unary published entry;\n- no second argument or truthy selector;\n- no `:clj/body` or other private callable on the descriptor;\n- dynamic admission outside statically proven intra-unit calls;\n- existing outcome, tail/non-tail, and operand-order semantics.\n\nIt removes D’s per-call `dsg__assoc` closure invocation and the map lookups for positional arguments, named arguments, and the token.\n\n### Acceptance requirements\n\n- Keep both the **2M instruction budget** and the **100,000 machine-data bound** unchanged.\n- Measure and report exact walker and semantic instruction counts for both formerly blocked fixtures.\n- Require `check-assume-have-discharge` to complete at 2M on both lanes, with the full gate reaching `102/2/2`.\n- Add adversarial tests applying the extracted public entry with forged vectors and confirming that none reaches the body’s outcome-forwarding lane.\n- Retain the descriptor-authenticity, shadowing, redefinition, error-outcome, and operand-order suites.\n- No `yin.vm` changes or shared-runtime review are authorized.\n\nIf D2 still exceeds 2M, return its exact completion counts. A 4M uniform bound—not a per-fixture table—can then be considered as a separate acceptance tradeoff with measured headroom. The gate remains honestly `:blocked` for the 20 unexercised arities regardless."}
